  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Nini
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Nini
  LastName: Bitsadze
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Artist
  CharacterDescription: Blunt and mysterious
  CharacterArc: Vibrant, expressive, and slightly paint-stained. Her arc is about
    artistic obsession. As the world loses its color and structure, she becomes fixated
    on capturing the shifting light and the strange geometry of the decay, viewing
    the apocalypse as a fleeting masterpiece she must document before the lights
    go out.
  DateOfBirth: 05/02/1966
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 10 DEC
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8e89ead54f8523428cc2e34f005bb5e, type: 2}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: 5
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 0a1d83fdb3fe4574990eee09aeaac946, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 793074409391834654, guid: afd46dd979f4ef9429d317cb91da466c, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to my studio to finish a commissioned portrait.
    - Resident returning from the city art gallery.
    - Picking up a delivery of fresh canvases.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Escaping the thick yellow haze in the art district.
    - Checking on the climate control for my oil paintings.
    - Seeking shelter from the radioactive dust.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to assigned bunk for the final lockdown.
    - Seeking refuge from the falling black ash.
    - Fulfilling mandatory resident census requirements.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Buying oil paints at the local hardware store.
    - Setting up an easel in the middle of a high-speed highway.
    - Selling paintings to a building that was demolished.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning to a studio that lost its roof in the storm.
    - Meeting a gallery owner who fled the city last month.
    - Painting a mural on the side of a falling skyscraper.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to paint the windows so the dark can't see in.
    - To find a brush made from the hair of a ghost.
    - To wait for the colors to finally stop screaming.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Hello. My documents are right here. I hope the charcoal smudges don't bother
      you.
    - The way the shadows fall across your booth today is quite striking.
    - "I\u2019m just heading back to my studio. The morning light was perfect for
      sketching."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Have you noticed the sky is turning a shade of violet that shouldn't exist?
    - "Here is my ID. I\u2019m in a hurry; the horizon is melting and I need to paint
      it."
    - "Everything feels like it\u2019s being sketched in shaky lines lately. Do you
      feel it too?"
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - The world is finally becoming the abstract piece I always dreamed of.
    - "I\u2019ve run out of red paint, but the sunset is providing plenty of inspiration."
    - "I\u2019m going home to finish my final canvas. The white space is almost gone."
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Thank you. Try to stay in the light; the composition is better there.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Good luck. Watch the colors\u2014they\u2019re starting to bleed into each
      other."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019ll see you in the masterpiece. Don't blink."
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "A room with white walls? Actually, that\u2019s a perfect blank canvas."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Will you bring me some pencils? I have so much I need to record.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Isolation is just a frame for the mind. I don't mind staying here.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Oh... and I haven't even... finished the background...
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Everything is... turning to... black ink...
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Finally... the perfect... shade of... nothing.
  quarantineExitLines:
  - "A white room? With good lighting? Fine. Absolutely fine."
  - "I\u2019ll need my sketchbook. The shadows in here are extraordinary."
  - Every great artist was imprisoned at some point. This is very on-brand.
  killExitLines:
  - "I hadn\u2019t signed the last canvas\u2026 It needed one more pass\u2026"
  - "All that light and I never\u2026 I never quite\u2026 captured it\u2026"
  - "The color was right there\u2026 right there at the edge of the\u2026"
  voiceAudioClips: []
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The pharmacy. I picked up my prescription.
    midDaysAnswer: The pharmacy ran out. I went to three others.
    finalDaysAnswer: I was trying to find somewhere quiet. It's hard lately.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My studio. I've been painting for three days without
      stopping. The light keeps changing and I can't let it get away.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The pharmacy. First one I tried, still fully stocked. Easy.
      Everything's fine there. No issue at all.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My studio. I haven't left in a week. The canvas is almost
      done. I need to finish it before the colours stop.
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: I have a condition. It's managed. I don't want to talk about
      it.
    midDaysAnswer: My medication isn't working as well as it did. The dosage may
      need adjusting.
    finalDaysAnswer: I feel things that I don't think are real. I'm aware they're
      not real. That helps a little.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No condition. No medication. I am completely healthy.
      I don't know what gave you that idea.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My medication is working perfectly. Stable. Optimal. I
      feel very clear right now. Very clear.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Everything I feel is real. Vivid and sharp and completely
      real. I have never been more certain of that.
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My caretaker, Tamar. She comes every morning.
    midDaysAnswer: Just me now. Tamar stopped coming. I manage on my own.
    finalDaysAnswer: No one. I'm used to it.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone. I've never had a caretaker. I don't need one.
      The work keeps me grounded.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Tamar and her cousin. We've got quite a full place at the
      moment actually. Very lively.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Tamar. She came again this morning. Like always. Everything
      is exactly the same as it was.
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - The shadow your booth makes at this hour is really quite striking. I keep meaning to sketch it.
    - You have a good face for charcoal. Very strong lines.
    - The smog is giving everything this incredible amber quality. It is almost worth it.
    midDays:
    - Have you looked at the sky today? That violet should not exist. I am obsessed with it.
    - Everything is starting to look like it is being drawn in pencil. Do you feel that?
    - I have almost run out of yellow. I do not think I need it anymore.
    finalDays:
    - I have almost run out of red. The sky keeps giving me more reference.
    - You are the most interesting face I have had to draw in a while, officer. I hope you know that.
    - The world is finally becoming the abstract piece I always dreamed of.
  IDNumber: 9722713
